Remember to call this function with PexRun under test code, instead of PexAssemblyInfo, if you want to actually test it. You should also use PexMethod under method signature.

This way you can test not only the logic of the code, but also its behavior with various inputs and edge cases. And you can see the expected and actual results for each test case in a user-friendly UI.

However, please note that Pex is not always 100% effective, and some edge cases or corner cases might be hard to test, especially in complex systems. The above code is just to give a basic idea on how to use Pex.

To get the most out of Pex, you should learn to read the tests it generates and use them as examples when creating your own tests.
